NAME
       chdir, getcwd - the working directory

SYNOPSIS
       #include <unistd.h>

       int   chdir(const char *path);
       int   fchdir(int fd);
       char *getcwd(char *buf, size_t size);

DESCRIPTION
       chdir changes the working directory of the calling process, and
       getcwd reports it as an absolute path. fchdir does the same
       given a descriptor for a directory.

       The directory is per-process and is inherited across fork and
       execve, so a child starts where its parent was.

RETURN VALUE
       chdir returns 0 or -1; getcwd returns BUF or NULL, with errno
       set on failure.

ERRORS
       ENOENT    the path does not exist
       ENOTDIR   a component is not a directory
       ERANGE    the buffer is too small

SEE ALSO
       pwd(1), csh(1)
